# INERT FOR THE CANONICAL BUILD. Read this before trusting it.
#
# Docker resolves .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT. The canonical build for this image
# is `docker build -f connectors/thalamus-square/Dockerfile -t square-connector .` run
# from the MONOREPO ROOT, so the file Docker reads is /.dockerignore, not this one.
# Nothing here has any effect on the shipped image. Verified empirically: this file
# lists tests/, and connectors/thalamus-square/tests was landing in the image anyway.
#
# (BuildKit does check one sibling location — `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`, i.e.
# `Dockerfile.dockerignore` in this directory. A bare `.dockerignore` is NOT that.)
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY BOUNDS THE IMAGE: the Dockerfile's explicit COPYs, plus /.dockerignore
# for anything that rides inside a copied directory (tests/, scripts/, .env*, the
# dev-only transport and its test doubles). Add exclusions THERE, not here.
#
# This file is kept only for a hypothetical directory-context build
# (`docker build connectors/thalamus-square`), which nothing does today.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
.env
.env.*
